==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From [[w:Henry Shrapnel|Henry Shrapnel]], British army officer who invented an anti-personnel shell that transported a large number of bullets to the target before releasing them, at a far greater distance than rifles could fire the bullets individually.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# a collective term for [[shot]], [[fragment]]s, or [[debris]] thrown out by an [[exploding]] [[shell]] or [[landmine]]
# {{slang}} [[loose change]]

